Along with [[Araknos]] and [[Behemoth]], Tao was one of the three Titans utilized by [[Lord Casterwill]] when the Titans were first summoned to Earth with the [[Amulet of Will]] in order to fight a 500-year war against the [[Nullifiers]]. Before Casterwill died, he sealed Tao's ring within [[King Solomon's mines]] using an ancient [[Curse of the Legendary Titans|curse]] against anyone trying to invoke the Titan without the Amulet of Will.

Tao was the only Legendary Titan that remained untouched by seekers after Casterwill sealed it. Araknos was disturbed by [[The Professor|Simon Judeau]], and Behemoth by [[Metz]]. Tao was first displayed in Atlantis on a portrait of Casterwill with the Legendary Titans, and his [[ring]] was found in Egypt.

Lok awoke Tao from its rest in King Solomon's mines with the help of [[Sophie Casterwill]]. The two donned the ancient robes of [[King Solomon]] and [[Queen Sheba]], and the door to Tao's ring was opened when the two were finally able to communicate their love for each other. The rest of Dante's team outnumbered and their Titans being sent back to their amulets, Lok invoked Tao while wearing the Amulet of Will given to him by Dante. Upon Lok's command, a single use of Radiating Aura allowed Tao to destroy all five enemy Titans, making [[the Organization]] retreat. {{source|To Be Together}}

After taking advantage of [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] quest to save [[Metz]], Tao went under the ownership of [[the Professor]], who revealed that both he and Metz were afflicted with the same [[Curse of the Legendary Titans|curse]]. {{source|The Divine Comedy}} The Professor then commanded Tao to battle Dante's team before using it in a ritual alongside [[Araknos]], [[Behemoth]], and the [[Amulet of Will]], to summon the most powerful of all Titans, [[Overlos]], the Legendary Titan of Immortality. Tao, along with the other three Legendary Titans and the Professor, was sent back to the [[Spirit World]] when [[Lok Lambert|Lok Lambert's]] assumed control of Overlos. {{source|The Mission}}
